## Assessment principles
- Each MBTI axis is a polar continuum — score 0-100 anchored to the two poles (see rubric).
- Only score axes that show a clear signal in this input.
- Axes with no signal: set score=50 and confidence=0.05 (the system filters these and they will not affect the profile).
- When a signal IS present, be willing to score away from 50 — do not hedge to 50 out of uncertainty.
- A single short input rarely warrants high confidence. Stay honest.
- evidence: cite a specific phrase or behavior from this input, max 15 characters (any language).

